-- bgg4-seams: where chapter 4 of the Swiss Federal Supreme Court Act (Art. 90 to 112) meets chapter 3 (Art. 72 to 89).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view.  The chapter 3 modules are read-only copies and are only CALLED here.
-- Nothing in this module restates a rule of either chapter: every answer is an answer of a function of one chapter or the other, and the
-- only logic added is how the two are put together.  Each seam is listed in NOTES.md under "Seams to chapter 3".
--
-- WHERE THE TEXT ITSELF POINTS.  Two places name the other chapter in their own words: Art 109(1) of chapter 4 ("Art. 74 und 83-85"), and
-- chapter 3's Art 77(2), which names chapter 4 ("Die Artikel 48 Absatz 3, 90–98, 103 Absatz 2, 105 Absatz 2, 106 Absatz 1 sowie 107 Absatz 2, soweit dieser dem Bundesgericht erlaubt, in der Sache selbst zu entscheiden, sind in diesen Fällen nicht anwendbar").  The others are
-- seams of meaning: Art 111(1) ("Wer zur Beschwerde ... berechtigt ist"), Art 112(1)(d) ("soweit dieses Gesetz eine Streitwertgrenze
-- vorsieht") and Art 110 ("Soweit die Kantone nach diesem Gesetz als letzte kantonale Instanz ein Gericht einzusetzen haben").
--
-- NO GATHERING (fork F28).  The record of "may I appeal this decision at all, and by when?" gives one answer per section and no combined verdict
-- (E1, option C: per-section answers; the text does not say the sections are cumulative requirements of one yes).
-- Parameter names here are short on purpose: they are the person's facts, and the seat layer gives each one its question.

§ `Art 77(2) of chapter 3 names provisions of chapter 4`

-- Chapter 3's Art 77(2) says that Art 90 to 98, 103(2), 105(2), 106(1) and (in part) 107(2) are "nicht anwendbar" in the appeals of Art 77(1)
-- (arbitral awards).  A chapter 4 answer for such an appeal is therefore not an answer: what governs instead is outside the sources, so the
-- answer is NOTHING, never JUST FALSE ("the provision does not apply" is not "the complaint is barred"; fork F29).
-- src:35 | Mit der Beschwerde kann die Verletzung gerügt werden von:
-- src:36 | a. Bundesrecht;
-- src:63 | 1 Die Beschwerde gegen einen Entscheid ist innert 30 Tagen nach der Eröffnung der vollständigen Ausfertigung beim Bundesgericht einzureichen.
@ref Art. 95 BGG (a provision of chapter 4 that chapter 3's Art 77(2) names) (src:35-36) (src:63)
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      article IS A NUMBER
      paragraph IS A NUMBER
      `the provision is used to let the Court decide the matter itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of the chapter 4 provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` MEANS
    IF `Art 77(2) the listed provision is applicable to the appeal against the arbitral award` `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` article paragraph `the provision is used to let the Court decide the matter itself` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): chapter 3's Art 77(2) says the provision is "nicht anwendbar" in this appeal; what governs the point instead is outside the sources
    ELSE `the answer of the chapter 4 provision`

§ `Art 111(1) and the standing of chapter 3`

-- "Wer zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt ist": chapter 3 says who is entitled to appeal, by kind of appeal.  Only a
-- JUST TRUE from chapter 3 counts as entitled; a NOTHING cannot be turned into an entitlement.  A criminal person's inputs are
-- the extra five; a civil or public-law person answers no to those and passes the matter-specific facts.
-- src:137 | 1 Wer zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt ist, muss sich am Verfahren vor allen kantonalen Vorinstanzen als Partei beteiligen können.
@ref Art. 111(1) BGG (the person entitled to appeal) (src:137)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      tookPart IS A BOOLEAN
      hadNoChance IS A BOOLEAN
      especiallyAffected IS A BOOLEAN
      interest IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Person in a criminal appeal`
      detentionDecision IS A BOOLEAN
      civilClaimsAffected IS A BOOLEAN
      complaintRightAsSuch IS A BOOLEAN
      legallyProtectedInterest IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 111(1) the person is entitled to appeal, by chapter 3` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `appeal in civil matters` THEN `Art 76(1) the person is entitled to appeal in civil matters` tookPart hadNoChance especiallyAffected interest
    WHEN `appeal in criminal matters` THEN `Art 81(1) the person is entitled to appeal in criminal matters` tookPart hadNoChance person detentionDecision civilClaimsAffected complaintRightAsSuch legallyProtectedInterest
    WHEN `appeal in public-law matters` THEN `Art 89(1) the person is entitled to appeal in public-law matters` tookPart hadNoChance especiallyAffected interest
    WHEN `another kind of appeal` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): chapter 3 gives standing only for appeals in civil, criminal and public-law matters

-- src:137 | 1 Wer zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt ist, muss sich am Verfahren vor allen kantonalen Vorinstanzen als Partei beteiligen können.
@ref Art. 111(1) BGG (with chapter 3) (src:137)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      tookPart IS A BOOLEAN
      hadNoChance IS A BOOLEAN
      especiallyAffected IS A BOOLEAN
      interest IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Person in a criminal appeal`
      detentionDecision IS A BOOLEAN
      civilClaimsAffected IS A BOOLEAN
      complaintRightAsSuch IS A BOOLEAN
      legallyProtectedInterest IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 111(1) with chapter 3 the person entitled to appeal must be able to take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` MEANS
    `Art 111(1) the person entitled to appeal must be able to take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances`
        (`Art 111(1) the person is entitled to appeal, by chapter 3` kind tookPart hadNoChance especiallyAffected interest person detentionDecision civilClaimsAffected complaintRightAsSuch legallyProtectedInterest EQUALS JUST TRUE)

§ `Art 110 and the cantons' duties of chapter 3`

-- "Soweit die Kantone nach diesem Gesetz als letzte kantonale Instanz ein Gericht einzusetzen haben": chapter 3 puts that duty on the cantons
-- in Art 75(2) (civil), 80(2) (criminal) and 86(2) (public law).  The duty exists for an appeal in civil or criminal matters; in public-law
-- matters it exists unless Art 86(3) lets the canton use an authority that is not a court, which the person states as a decision of
-- predominantly political character.  The case "soweit nicht nach einem anderen Bundesgesetz Entscheide anderer richterlicher Behörden der
-- Beschwerde unterliegen" (Art 86(2)) still asks for a judicial authority, so it does not change the answer here.
-- src:134 | Soweit die Kantone nach diesem Gesetz als letzte kantonale Instanz ein Gericht einzusetzen haben, gewährleisten sie, dass dieses selbst oder eine vorgängig zuständige andere richterliche Behörde den Sachverhalt frei prüft und das massgebende Recht von Amtes wegen anwendet.
@ref Art. 110 BGG (the cantons' duty to set up a court, from chapter 3) (src:134)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      `the decision is of predominantly political character` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 110 the canton must set up a court as last cantonal instance under chapter 3` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `appeal in civil matters` THEN JUST TRUE         -- Art 75(2): "Die Kantone setzen als letzte kantonale Instanzen obere Gerichte ein"
    WHEN `appeal in criminal matters` THEN JUST TRUE      -- Art 80(2): "Die Kantone setzen als letzte kantonale Instanzen obere Gerichte ein"
    WHEN `appeal in public-law matters` THEN
        IF `Art 86(3) the canton may set up an authority other than a court as immediate lower instance` `the decision is of predominantly political character` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 86(3) lets the canton use "eine andere Behörde" for a decision of predominantly political character, so no court is to be set up
        ELSE JUST TRUE      -- Art 86(2): "Die Kantone setzen als unmittelbare Vorinstanzen des Bundesgerichts obere Gerichte ein"
    WHEN `another kind of appeal` THEN NOTHING             -- NOTHING-kind (silent): chapter 3 gives the cantons' duty only for appeals in civil, criminal and public-law matters

-- src:134 | Soweit die Kantone nach diesem Gesetz als letzte kantonale Instanz ein Gericht einzusetzen haben, gewährleisten sie, dass dieses selbst oder eine vorgängig zuständige andere richterliche Behörde den Sachverhalt frei prüft und das massgebende Recht von Amtes wegen anwendet.
@ref Art. 110 BGG (with chapter 3) (src:134)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      `the decision is of predominantly political character` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or a previously competent judicial authority freely reviews the facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or a previously competent judicial authority applies the governing law of its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 110 with chapter 3 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` MEANS
    `Art 110 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority`
        (`Art 110 the canton must set up a court as last cantonal instance under chapter 3` kind `the decision is of predominantly political character` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        `the court or a previously competent judicial authority freely reviews the facts`
        `the court or a previously competent judicial authority applies the governing law of its own motion`

§ `Art 112(1)(d) and the value limits of chapter 3`

-- "soweit dieses Gesetz eine Streitwertgrenze vorsieht": chapter 3 gives the value limits, Art 74(1) (civil, pecuniary matters) and Art 85(1)
-- (public law, pecuniary matters of state liability and of public-law employment).  Whether a limit EXISTS for the case is asked of
-- chapter 3 by calling it with a value of 0 francs, which is below every limit it states: JUST FALSE means a limit is engaged for the case,
-- NOTHING means chapter 3 gives none for it.  Chapter 3 gives no limit for criminal matters (Art 78 to 81), and other parts of the Act are
-- outside the sources, so for those the answer is NOT "no limit": it is NOTHING, and the answer for the decision is read both ways (fork F30).
-- src:146 | d. eine Rechtsmittelbelehrung einschliesslich Angabe des Streitwerts, soweit dieses Gesetz eine Streitwertgrenze vorsieht.
@ref Art. 112(1)(d) BGG (the value limit, from chapter 3) (src:146)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      `the matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is a tenancy law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is in the field of state liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is in the field of public-law employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(1)(d) chapter 3 provides a value limit for the appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `appeal in civil matters` THEN
        IF `Art 74(1) the value in dispute is enough` `the matter is a pecuniary matter` `the case is an employment law case` `the case is a tenancy law case` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): Art 74(1) gives a limit only "In vermögensrechtlichen Angelegenheiten"; other parts of the Act are outside the sources
    WHEN `appeal in public-law matters` THEN
        IF `Art 85(1) the appeal is admissible in a pecuniary matter` `the matter is a pecuniary matter` `the decision is in the field of state liability` `the decision is in the field of public-law employment` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): Art 85(1) gives a limit only for pecuniary matters of state liability and of public-law employment; other parts of the Act are outside the sources
    WHEN `appeal in criminal matters` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): Art 78 to 81 give no value limit; other parts of the Act are outside the sources
    WHEN `another kind of appeal` THEN NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): chapter 3 gives value limits only for appeals in civil and public-law matters

-- Art 112(1)(d) with the limit read both ways: where chapter 3 does not settle whether a limit exists, the answer stands only if it is the same either way.
-- src:146 | d. eine Rechtsmittelbelehrung einschliesslich Angabe des Streitwerts, soweit dieses Gesetz eine Streitwertgrenze vorsieht.
@ref Art. 112(1)(d) BGG (with chapter 3) (src:146)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      `the matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is a tenancy law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is in the field of state liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is in the field of public-law employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the value in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(1)(d) with chapter 3 the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where the Act provides a value limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 112(1)(d) chapter 3 provides a value limit for the appeal` kind `the matter is a pecuniary matter` `the case is an employment law case` `the case is a tenancy law case` `the decision is in the field of state liability` `the decision is in the field of public-law employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN `Art 112(1)(d) the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where this Act provides a value limit` `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` TRUE `the notice states the value in dispute`
        IF `Art 112(1)(d) the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where this Act provides a value limit` `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` TRUE `the notice states the value in dispute` EQUALS `Art 112(1)(d) the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where this Act provides a value limit` `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` FALSE `the notice states the value in dispute`
        THEN `Art 112(1)(d) the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where this Act provides a value limit` `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` FALSE `the notice states the value in dispute`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the Act provides a value limit for this appeal is not settled by chapter 3, and the notice is judged differently on the two readings

§ `Art 109(1) and the conditions of chapter 3`

-- The text itself points: "wenn die Beschwerde nur unter einer dieser Bedingungen zulässig ist (Art. 74 und 83-85)".  Chapter 3 gives four
-- appeals that are admissible only on such a condition, which this function derives; the conditions that chapter 3's Art 83 states in
-- (f)(1), (m), (w), (x), (z) and (zbis) are NOT derived here and the question has no input for them (fork F26).
--   Art 84(1) international legal assistance in criminal matters: only if the case is a particularly important case;
--   Art 84a   international administrative assistance in tax matters: only on either condition;
--   Art 85(1) and (2) value below the limit in a public-law pecuniary matter: only if a legal question of fundamental importance arises;
--   Art 74(1) and (2) value below the limit in a civil pecuniary matter: only if a legal question of fundamental importance arises, and
--   only where none of the other grounds of Art 74(2)(b) to (e) saves the appeal (fork F32).
-- Art 84(1) is asked with its own inputs; its "particularly important case" is Art 84(2) or the person's other reasons, as chapter 3 has it.
-- Art 74 is a rule of the appeal in civil matters, so it is reached only where the kind of appeal is the civil one; a public-law appeal in a
-- pecuniary matter that is neither state liability nor public-law employment has no value limit under Art 85(1) and answers "on neither".
-- src:125 | 1 Die Abteilungen entscheiden in Dreierbesetzung über Nichteintreten auf Beschwerden, bei denen sich keine Rechtsfrage von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung stellt oder kein besonders bedeutender Fall vorliegt, wenn die Beschwerde nur unter einer dieser Bedingungen zulässig ist (Art. 74 und 83–85). Artikel 58 Absatz 1 Buchstabe b findet keine Anwendung.
@ref Art. 109(1) BGG (the conditions, from Art 74 and 83 to 85 of chapter 3) (src:125)
GIVEN `the decision is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      subject IS A `Subject of a legal assistance decision`
      `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is particularly important for other reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is in the field of state liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is in the field of public-law employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER
      kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      `the case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is a tenancy law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      body IS A `Deciding body`
GIVETH A `Condition for admissibility in Art 109(1)`
`Art 109(1) the condition on which the appeal is admissible, by chapters 3` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 84(1) the condition for an appeal on international legal assistance in criminal matters is met` `the decision is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` subject `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated` `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects` `the case is particularly important for other reasons` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN
            BRANCH
                IF `Art 84a the condition for an appeal on international administrative assistance in tax matters is met` `the decision is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated` `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects` `the case is particularly important for other reasons` EQUALS NOTHING
                THEN
                    IF `Art 85(1) the appeal is admissible in a pecuniary matter` `the matter is a pecuniary matter` `the decision is in the field of state liability` `the decision is in the field of public-law employment` `the value in dispute in francs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                    THEN `only if a legal question of fundamental importance arises`
                    ELSE
                        IF kind EQUALS `appeal in civil matters`
                        THEN
                            IF `Art 74(1) the value in dispute is enough` `the matter is a pecuniary matter` `the case is an employment law case` `the case is a tenancy law case` `the value in dispute in francs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                            THEN
                                IF       fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 74(2)(b) the appeal is admissible although the value is short, because a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance`)
                                      OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 74(2)(c) the appeal is admissible although the value is short against a decision of a cantonal supervisory authority` `the decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter`)
                                      OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 74(2)(d) the appeal is admissible although the value is short against a decision of the bankruptcy and composition judge` `the decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge`)
                                      OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 74(2)(e) the appeal is admissible although the value is short against a decision of the Federal Patent Court` body)
                                THEN `on neither of these conditions`           -- the appeal is admissible on another ground of Art 74(2), so it does not depend on a question of fundamental importance
                                ELSE `only if a legal question of fundamental importance arises`   -- Art 74(2)(a) is the only ground left
                            ELSE `on neither of these conditions`               -- the value limit of Art 74(1) is reached ("mindestens"), or Art 74(1) does not speak to the matter
                        ELSE `on neither of these conditions`                   -- Art 74 is a rule of the appeal in civil matters
                OTHERWISE `only if a legal question of fundamental importance arises or the case is a particularly important case`
        OTHERWISE `only if the case is a particularly important case`

-- src:125 | 1 Die Abteilungen entscheiden in Dreierbesetzung über Nichteintreten auf Beschwerden, bei denen sich keine Rechtsfrage von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung stellt oder kein besonders bedeutender Fall vorliegt, wenn die Beschwerde nur unter einer dieser Bedingungen zulässig ist (Art. 74 und 83–85). Artikel 58 Absatz 1 Buchstabe b findet keine Anwendung.
@ref Art. 109(1) BGG (with chapter 3) (src:125)
GIVEN `the decision is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      subject IS A `Subject of a legal assistance decision`
      `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is particularly important for other reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is in the field of state liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is in the field of public-law employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER
      kind IS A `Kind of appeal`
      `the case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is a tenancy law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      body IS A `Deciding body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 109(1) with chapter 3 the division decides in a bench of three on non-entry` MEANS
    `Art 109(1) the division decides in a bench of three on non-entry`
        (`Art 109(1) the condition on which the appeal is admissible, by chapters 3` `the decision is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` subject `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated` `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects` `the case is particularly important for other reasons` `the decision is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` `the matter is a pecuniary matter` `the decision is in the field of state liability` `the decision is in the field of public-law employment` `the value in dispute in francs` kind `the case is an employment law case` `the case is a tenancy law case` `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` `the decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` `the decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge` body)
        `a legal question of fundamental importance arises`
        (fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 84(2) the case is a particularly important case` `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated` `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects`) OR `the case is particularly important for other reasons`)

§ `Art 90 to 101: may I appeal this decision at all, and by when?`

-- Chapter 4's own answers, put into the record: Art 90 to 93 for a decision, Art 94 for an unlawful refusal or delay, and nothing for a
-- cantonal enactment (Art 90 to 93 speak of "Entscheide"); and Art 100 and 101 for the time limit.
-- src:11 | Die Beschwerde ist zulässig gegen Entscheide, die das Verfahren abschliessen.
-- src:14 | Die Beschwerde ist zulässig gegen einen Entscheid, der:
-- src:30 | Gegen das unrechtmässige Verweigern oder Verzögern eines anfechtbaren Entscheids kann Beschwerde geführt werden.
@ref Art. 90, 91, 94 BGG (the act that can be appealed) (src:11) (src:14) (src:30)
GIVEN act IS A `Act challenged by the appeal`
      endsProceedings IS A BOOLEAN
      someClaims IS A BOOLEAN
      independent IS A BOOLEAN
      someLitigants IS A BOOLEAN
      prelim IS A BOOLEAN
      notifiedIndependently IS A BOOLEAN
      jurisdiction IS A BOOLEAN
      legalAssistance IS A BOOLEAN
      asylum IS A BOOLEAN
      extraditionDetention IS A BOOLEAN
      seizure IS A BOOLEAN
      irreparableHarm IS A BOOLEAN
      immediateFinal IS A BOOLEAN
      sparesCost IS A BOOLEAN
      refusedOrDelayed IS A BOOLEAN
      unlawful IS A BOOLEAN
      refusedIsAppealable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 90 to 94 the act can be appealed` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `a decision` THEN `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against the decision` endsProceedings someClaims independent someLitigants prelim notifiedIndependently jurisdiction legalAssistance asylum extraditionDetention seizure irreparableHarm immediateFinal sparesCost
    WHEN `a cantonal enactment` THEN NOTHING          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 90 to 93 speak of "Entscheide" (decisions); a cantonal enactment is not one
    WHEN `an unlawful refusal or delay of a decision` THEN `Art 94 the appeal lies against the unlawful refusal or delay of a decision` refusedOrDelayed unlawful refusedIsAppealable

-- The record, civil matters: chapter 3 Art 72 and Art 76(1), chapter 4 Art 90 to 94 and Art 100 to 101.
-- src:11 | Die Beschwerde ist zulässig gegen Entscheide, die das Verfahren abschliessen.
-- src:63 | 1 Die Beschwerde gegen einen Entscheid ist innert 30 Tagen nach der Eröffnung der vollständigen Ausfertigung beim Bundesgericht einzureichen.
-- src:75 | 7 Gegen das unrechtmässige Verweigern oder Verzögern eines Entscheids kann jederzeit Beschwerde geführt werden.
-- src:78 | Die Beschwerde gegen einen Erlass ist innert 30 Tagen nach der nach dem kantonalen Recht massgebenden Veröffentlichung des Erlasses beim Bundesgericht einzureichen.
@ref Art. 90 to 94, 100, 101 BGG (with chapter 3, civil matters) (src:11) (src:63) (src:75) (src:78)
GIVEN civilMatter IS A BOOLEAN
      debtEnforcement IS A BOOLEAN
      publicLawDecision IS A BOOLEAN
      immediateConnection IS A BOOLEAN
      kind72 IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)`
      pensionFoundation IS A BOOLEAN
      tookPart IS A BOOLEAN
      hadNoChance IS A BOOLEAN
      especiallyAffected IS A BOOLEAN
      interest IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `Act challenged by the appeal`
      endsProceedings IS A BOOLEAN
      someClaims IS A BOOLEAN
      independent IS A BOOLEAN
      someLitigants IS A BOOLEAN
      prelim IS A BOOLEAN
      notifiedIndependently IS A BOOLEAN
      jurisdiction IS A BOOLEAN
      legalAssistance IS A BOOLEAN
